💻 Python for Genomics and Bioinformatics
Research Question
How can Python be used to analyse, visualise, and interpret genomic and biological data to answer research questions in genomics, bioinformatics, and computational biology?

🌊 Background
Modern genomics generates vast quantities of biological data that require computational approaches for analysis and interpretation. Python has become one of the most widely used programming languages in bioinformatics due to its versatility, extensive scientific libraries, and ability to automate complex workflows.
Bioinformaticians use Python to process genomic data, analyse gene expression, investigate evolutionary relationships, visualise biological patterns, and develop reproducible research pipelines.
This project documents my development of Python skills for applications in genomics, bioinformatics, evolutionary biology, and computational research.

🧬 Why This Matters
Computational skills are increasingly essential in modern biological research.
Python enables researchers to:
Analyse large genomic datasets
Automate repetitive tasks
Visualise complex biological data
Process sequencing results
Build reproducible workflows
Support data-driven scientific discovery

